   "subject": "Interpretation of IRT model formulas on 'package mirt’ documentation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Hi all,</font><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Sorry if this is a very basic question. Could I ask how to interpret the IRT formulas presented on p.99 of the &#39;Package mirt&#39; documentation (</font><a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirt/mirt.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirt/mirt.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472775807000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0F8keiNTq84skbzL-HyHqr\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirt/mirt.pdf</a>)<span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">? To focus on one, below is the 4pl formula provided:</span></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/attach/4574e2d104a3e/4pl%20formula.PNG?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"4pl formula.PNG\" width=\"320\" height=\"47\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\"></font></p><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">As I understand it:</font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> - P gives the probability </font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> - x=1 refers to 1 person </font></div><div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13.91px\"> - </span><span style=\"line-height:13.91px\">theta </span><span style=\"line-height:13.91px\">represents ability </span></font></div></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> - g represents guessing</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> - u represents fatigue</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> - a represents the item level\r\ncoefficient</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> - d represents the group level coefficient</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"> - exp denotes employment of the exponential function</span><br></div><div><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I think the above is correct, but please let me know if not! </font></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">However, I have seen the symbol</font></span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;line-height:107%\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">ψ used in various ways in IRT literature. E.g., the &quot;collection of all item parameters&quot; (Chalmers, 2012) and variance of the factor (MPlus guidance). Otherwise, this symbol might typically refer to the functional form (i.e., logistic).</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">How should I interpret the </span><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">ψ </span><span style=\"line-height:13.91px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">symbol</font></span><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.91px\"> in the above 4pl formula?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.91px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.91px\">Also, what do subscript 1 and subscript 2 denote in this formula?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.91px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.91px\">Thanks very much in advance and apologies for my lack of general understanding,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.91px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.91px\">Joe</span></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
